      "title": "The Revolt of Care: Anarchist Mutual Aid in 21st Century",
      "description": "The death of God did not free us from domination. It tore the social fabric, emboldened the profiteers, and left us alone in front of a silent, cold, and indifferent universe: the capitalist universe. Traditional communities were dissolved, and what replaced them was not the insurgent commune but the depression of the isolated nuclear family and the loneliness of the careerist. Our societies have not rejected the need for tenderness and care. They have covered it with a hard irony that makes it look unnecessary, naive, obsolete. Anxiety, precarity, debt and exhaustion are handed back to us as individual failures, and the loneliness that follows is not an accident of the system but one of its",
